# peeryard patch ergo/007: Do not request announced ADProofs on a node that stores the UTXO set
# upstream: ergoplatform/ergo#2585 (proposed); origin, witness and responses in patches.json
commit a65341679b59f9f667daed340a3bd51e5c1c6423
Author: cafebedouin <cafebedouin@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Sep 26 08:44:06 2026 -0500

    Do not request announced ADProofs on a node that stores the UTXO set
    
    The scheduler leaves UTXO set transformation proofs out when the UTXO set is stored (requiredModifiersForHeader):
    such a node regenerates them when it applies a block and keeps them for the recent suffix (UtxoState). The
    announcement path still requested them from peers, so a UTXO node downloaded proofs it would generate itself. It
    now ignores ADProofs announcements. Announcements are unchanged: the node holds the regenerated proofs and serves
    them.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/scala/org/ergoplatform/network/ErgoNodeViewSynchronizer.scala b/src/main/scala/org/ergoplatform/network/ErgoNodeViewSynchronizer.scala
